aints raised by customers regarding their experience or security-related issues.\"},\"attributes\":[{\"type\":\"integer\",\"name\":\"Customer ID\",\"description\":\"The attribute 'Customer ID: integer between 1 and 10000' represents the unique identification number assigned to each customer within the store system.\",\"min_value\":1,\"max_value\":10000,\"enumeration_values\":null},{\"type\":\"enumeration\",\"name\":\"Complaint Status\",\"description\":\"The attribute 'Complaint Status: Resolved, Unresolved' specifies the current resolution state of a customer complaint, indicating whether it has been resolved or remains unresolved.\",\"min_value\":null,\"max_value\":null,\"enumeration_values\":[\"Resolved\",\"Unresolved\"]}],\"description\":\"The bind 'Handle Customer Complaint: Customer ID, Complaint Status' links the 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity with the attributes 'Customer ID' and 'Complaint Status', specifying that handling a complaint requires identifying the customer and tracking the resolution status of the complaint.\"},{\"activity\":{\"name\":\"Perform Security Audit\",\"description\":\"The 'Perform Security Audit' activity entails conducting a comprehensive assessment of the store's security measures and assigning an audit score based on the findings.\"},\"attributes\":[{\"type\":\"float\",\"name\":\"Audit Score\",\"description\":\"The attribute 'Audit Score: float between 0.0 and 100.0' represents the score achieved during a security audit, reflecting the overall effectiveness of the store's security measures.\",\"min_value\":0.0,\"max_value\":100.0,\"enumeration_values\":null}],\"description\":\"The bind 'Perform Security Audit: Audit Score' links the 'Perform Security Audit' activity with the attribute 'Audit Score', specifying that performing a security audit requires recording the resulting audit score.\"},{\"activity\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Bag Check\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Bag Check' activity involves checking the bags of customers or visitors to prevent unauthorized items from entering or leaving the store.\"},\"attributes\":[{\"type\":\"integer\",\"name\":\"Customer ID\",\"description\":\"The attribute 'Customer ID: integer between 1 and 10000' represents the unique identification number assigned to each customer within the store system.\",\"min_value\":1,\"max_value\":10000,\"enumeration_values\":null}],\"description\":\"The bind 'Conduct Bag Check: Customer ID' links the 'Conduct Bag Check' activity with the attribute 'Customer ID', specifying that conducting a bag check requires identifying the customer whose bag is being checked.\"}],\"constraints\":[{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Monitor Store Entrance' activity must be the first activity to occur in the process.\",\"template\":\"Init\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Monitor Store Entrance\",\"description\":\"The 'Monitor Store Entrance' activity involves observing and surveilling the entrance area of the store to ensure security and detect any suspicious activity.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Deactivate Alarm' activity must be the last activity to occur in the process.\",\"template\":\"End\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Deactivate Alarm\",\"description\":\"The 'Deactivate Alarm' activity consists of turning off an active alarm system once the situation has been assessed and resolved.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity must occur at least once in the process.\",\"template\":\"Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity entails documenting and formally reporting a security incident, including its severity and type, for record-keeping and follow-up.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":1},{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Emergency Drill' activity must not occur in the process.\",\"template\":\"Absence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Emergency Drill\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Emergency Drill' activity involves organizing and executing a simulated emergency scenario to prepare staff for real emergency situations.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":1},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If an 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity occurs, then a 'Review Security Footage' activity must eventually occur after the 'Inspect Security Cameras' event at some point in the same process instance, provided that the 'Camera ID' attribute of the 'Inspect Security Cameras' event matches the 'Camera ID' attribute of the 'Review Security Footage' event. There is no requirement on how soon or what events may occur in between. Multiple 'Inspect Security Cameras' events can be pending at the same time, and a single 'Review Security Footage' event can fulfill the obligation for all preceding 'Inspect Security Cameras' events. If 'Inspect Security Cameras' does not occur, the constraint imposes no obligation on the occurrence of 'Review Security Footage'.\",\"template\":\"Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Inspect Security Cameras\",\"description\":\"The 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity entails reviewing and examining the security camera feeds to monitor ongoing activities within the store.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Review Security Footage\",\"description\":\"The 'Review Security Footage' activity involves analyzing previously recorded security camera footage to investigate incidents or verify events.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Camera ID == T.Camera ID\",\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"Whenever an 'Alert Security Personnel' activity occurs with the activation condition that the 'Security Level' is 'High', it must be immediately followed by an 'Escort Suspect' activity in the next event position, with no other events in between. Additionally, the 'Personnel ID' attribute of the 'Alert Security Personnel' event must match the 'Personnel ID' attribute of the 'Escort Suspect' event. This immediate succession must occur within 0 to 5 minutes. Multiple 'Alert Security Personnel'-'Escort Suspect' pairs can exist in a process instance, each adhering to this immediate succession rule. The 'Escort Suspect' activity is allowed to happen elsewhere in the process but not between an 'Alert Security Personnel' event and its corresponding 'Escort Suspect' event.\",\"template\":\"Chain Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Alert Security Personnel\",\"description\":\"The 'Alert Security Personnel' activity consists of notifying security staff about a potential security threat or incident requiring immediate attention.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Escort Suspect\",\"description\":\"The 'Escort Suspect' activity involves accompanying a suspected individual within or out of the store premises while maintaining security protocols.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Security Level is High\",\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Personnel ID == T.Personnel ID\",\"time_condition\":\"0,5,m\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Alert Security Personnel' activity can occur only if it is immediately preceded by a 'Verify Alarm Trigger' activity, with no other activities occurring in between. This constraint applies when the activation condition specifies that the 'Alarm Status' is 'Triggered'. The time condition requires that the 'Alert Security Personnel' activity must occur within 0 to 10 minutes after the preceding 'Verify Alarm Trigger' event. There can be multiple 'Verify Alarm Trigger'-'Alert Security Personnel' pairs within the process, each adhering to this immediate precedence rule.\",\"template\":\"Chain Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Alert Security Personnel\",\"description\":\"The 'Alert Security Personnel' activity consists of notifying security staff about a potential security threat or incident requiring immediate attention.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Verify Alarm Trigger\",\"description\":\"The 'Verify Alarm Trigger' activity consists of confirming whether an alarm activation is genuine or a false alarm by inspecting the relevant alarm status.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Alarm Status is Triggered\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":\"0,10,m\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If a 'Perform Security Audit' activity occurs with the activation condition that the 'Audit Score' is less than 50, then an 'Update Security Protocols' activity must also occur in the same process instance, and vice versa. This mutual obligation ensures that neither event can occur without the other when the audit score is below 50. The events can occur multiple times and in any order relative to each other. If neither event occurs, the constraint is still considered satisfied.\",\"template\":\"Co-Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Perform Security Audit\",\"description\":\"The 'Perform Security Audit' activity entails conducting a comprehensive assessment of the store's security measures and assigning an audit score based on the findings.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Update Security Protocols\",\"description\":\"The 'Update Security Protocols' activity involves revising and improving the existing security procedures and guidelines to enhance store safety.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Audit Score < 50\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Conduct Bag Check' activity must be followed by a 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity at some point later in the same process instance, provided that the 'Customer ID' attribute of the 'Conduct Bag Check' event matches the 'Customer ID' attribute of the 'Handle Customer Complaint' event. Conversely, a 'Handle Customer Complaint' event can occur only if a 'Conduct Bag Check' event has occurred before it within the same process instance. This bidirectional and ordered dependency must be satisfied within 0 to 1 hour. Multiple 'Conduct Bag Check' and 'Handle Customer Complaint' events are allowed, with each 'Conduct Bag Check' eventually leading to a 'Handle Customer Complaint' and each 'Handle Customer Complaint' being justified by a preceding 'Conduct Bag Check'.\",\"template\":\"Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Bag Check\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Bag Check' activity involves checking the bags of customers or visitors to prevent unauthorized items from entering or leaving the store.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Handle Customer Complaint\",\"description\":\"The 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity involves receiving, processing, and resolving complaints raised by customers regarding their experience or security-related issues.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Customer ID == T.Customer ID\",\"time_condition\":\"0,1,h\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' activity cannot be immediately followed by a 'Report Incident' activity; there must be at least one other event between them. Similarly, a 'Report Incident' event cannot be immediately preceded by a 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' event. This constraint allows multiple occurrences of 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' and 'Report Incident' in any order, provided they are not adjacent in the event sequence.\",\"template\":\"Not Chain Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Check Inventory Discrepancies\",\"description\":\"The 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' activity entails investigating mismatches or inconsistencies in the store's inventory records to identify potential theft or errors.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity entails documenting and formally reporting a security incident, including its severity and type, for record-keeping and follow-up.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"Exactly one of the activities 'Train Security Staff' or 'Conduct Emergency Drill' must occur in the process instance. This means that the process is compliant if only 'Train Security Staff' occurs without any occurrence of 'Conduct Emergency Drill', or only 'Conduct Emergency Drill' occurs without any occurrence of 'Train Security Staff'. The process is non-compliant if both 'Train Security Staff' and 'Conduct Emergency Drill' occur, or if neither occurs. The constraint enforces a mutual exclusivity and a mandatory occurrence of one of the specified activities.\",\"template\":\"Exclusive Choice\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Train Security Staff\",\"description\":\"The 'Train Security Staff' activity consists of providing training sessions to security personnel to ensure they are equipped with the necessary skills and knowledge.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Emergency Drill\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Emergency Drill' activity involves organizing and executing a simulated emergency scenario to prepare staff for real emergency situations.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity is permitted to occur only if an 'Escort Suspect' activity has occurred before it within the same process instance, provided that the 'Incident Type' attribute of the 'Report Incident' event is 'Theft'. 'Report Incident' events that occur without any prior 'Escort Suspect' are violations of the constraint. Multiple 'Escort Suspect' events can occur, and any number of events can happen between an 'Escort Suspect' and a subsequent 'Report Incident'.\",\"template\":\"Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity entails documenting and formally reporting a security incident, including its severity and type, for record-keeping and follow-up.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Escort Suspect\",\"description\":\"The 'Escort Suspect' activity involves accompanying a suspected individual within or out of the store premises while maintaining security protocols.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":\"T.Incident Type is Theft\",\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Verify Alarm Trigger' activity cannot be preceded by a 'Deactivate Alarm' activity within the same process instance. This means that if any 'Deactivate Alarm' event has occurred before a 'Verify Alarm Trigger' event, then 'Verify Alarm Trigger' is disallowed. Multiple instances of 'Verify Alarm Trigger' and 'Deactivate Alarm' can occur, but all instances of 'Verify Alarm Trigger' must occur before any instance of 'Deactivate Alarm'.\",\"template\":\"Not Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Verify Alarm Trigger\",\"description\":\"The 'Verify Alarm Trigger' activity consists of confirming whether an alarm activation is genuine or a false alarm by inspecting the relevant alarm status.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Deactivate Alarm\",\"description\":\"The 'Deactivate Alarm' activity consists of turning off an active alarm system once the situation has been assessed and resolved.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If a 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity occurs with the activation condition that the 'Complaint Status' is 'Resolved', then a 'Conduct Bag Check' activity must not occur anywhere in the same process instance, provided that the 'Customer ID' attribute of the 'Handle Customer Complaint' event matches the 'Customer ID' attribute of the 'Conduct Bag Check' event. This means that the occurrence of 'Handle Customer Complaint' with a resolved status prohibits any occurrence of 'Conduct Bag Check' for the same customer. However, if 'Handle Customer Complaint' does not occur, 'Conduct Bag Check' may occur freely. Multiple occurrences of 'Handle Customer Complaint' are allowed, provided 'Conduct Bag Check' does not occur at all for the same customer in the process instance.\",\"template\":\"Not Responded Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Handle Customer Complaint\",\"description\":\"The 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity involves receiving, processing, and resolving complaints raised by customers regarding their experience or security-related issues.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Bag Check\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Bag Check' activity involves checking the bags of customers or visitors to prevent unauthorized items from entering or leaving the store.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Complaint Status is Resolved\",\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Customer ID == T.Customer ID\",\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Review Security Footage' activity and an 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity must not occur such that the 'Review Security Footage' event is followed by the 'Inspect Security Cameras' event at any point later in the same process instance. Similarly, an 'Inspect Security Cameras' event must not be preceded by a 'Review Security Footage' event. This means that once a 'Review Security Footage' occurs, 'Inspect Security Cameras' cannot occur afterward, and if an 'Inspect Security Cameras' event occurs, it cannot have been preceded by a 'Review Security Footage' event. Both events can occur in the same process instance, but not in the prohibited sequence.\",\"template\":\"Not Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Review Security Footage\",\"description\":\"The 'Review Security Footage' activity involves analyzing previously recorded security camera footage to investigate incidents or verify events.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Inspect Security Cameras\",\"description\":\"The 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity entails reviewing and examining the security camera feeds to monitor ongoing activities within the store.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null}]}"